    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0279" n="265" xml:id="pg265"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/8–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-08T15:00:00-04:00">August 8, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6254. The President has now approved the surrender instrument for Germany and you
                    are therefore authorized to inform the European Advisory Commission that the
                    American Government agrees to the instrument as recommended by the
                    Commission.</p>
                <p>For your confidential information, the President has indicated his desire that
                    China be given an opportunity to approve the surrender instrument without,
                    however, making China a party thereto. The Department will therefore make
                    available to representatives of the Chinese Government here for their
                    confidential information the text of the terms and will inform you subsequently
                    of the Chinese reaction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
